//- STRUCTURE AND MOTION: dividers, the spine, auto-animate, transitions and links.

section.divider(data-timing="0")
  h2 Structure
  p Dividers, the spine, and things that move.
  p templates/_divider.scss, layout/_spine.scss, motion/

//- A divider, then a section on the spine. The first slide has no band, so it grows in when the second arrives (js/spine.js).
section

  section.divider(data-timing="0")
    h2 Part two
    p A new side of the tape.
    p.fragment The promise sits low on the right.
    aside.notes
      ul
        li section.divider: the Mustard field floods the left 40%, the name sits high in it, the promise low on the right. Never count with it.

  section.statement(data-auto-animate data-timing="0")
    h2 A section about one thing.
    p.aside (watch the left edge)
    aside.notes
      ul
        li No spine yet. The next slide grows one in.

  section.has-spine(data-auto-animate data-timing="0")
    .spine-tag
      p.spine-number(data-id="SpineNumber") 01
      code.spine-label(data-id="SpineLabel") one thing
    h3 The spine carries the summary
    p A number at the top, a label running up the band.
    aside.notes
      ul
        li .has-spine on every slide of the section, with a .spine-tag holding p.spine-number and .spine-label. Only for a section that's about one thing.

  section.has-spine(data-auto-animate data-timing="0")
    .spine-tag
      p.spine-number(data-id="SpineNumber") 01
      code.spine-label(data-id="SpineLabel") one thing
    h3 And it holds still
    p Matched by data-id, the number and label stay put while the content changes.
    aside.notes
      ul
        li data-auto-animate on each slide, data-id on the number and label.

//- Auto-animate: match text by data-id on a p, heading or li and it moves crisply.
section

  section(data-auto-animate data-timing="0")
    h3 Auto-animate
    ul
      li(data-id="First") First
      li(data-id="Second") Second
      li(data-id="Third") Third
    aside.notes
      ul
        li data-auto-animate on both slides, data-id on each li. Match text on a p, heading or li so only its font-size animates.

  section(data-auto-animate data-timing="0")
    h3 Auto-animate
    ul
      li(data-id="Third") Third
      li(data-id="First") First
      li(data-id="Second") Second
      li Fourth, rising in unmatched

//- Transitions: Lemon's dissolve is the default; a slide can still ask reveal for another.
section

  section(data-timing="0")
    h3 Every slide dissolves
    p The lemon transition, set in js/reveal-config.js.
    aside.notes
      ul
        li transition: "lemon". motion/_transitions.scss.

  section(data-transition="zoom" data-timing="0")
    h2 Unless it asks for something else.
    aside.notes
      ul
        li data-transition="zoom" (or fade, slide, convex, concave). Lemon's rules step aside for any slide with data-transition.

  section(data-timing="0")
    h3 Internal links
    p
      a(href="#/CatalogueCode") Jump back to the code examples.
    aside.notes
      ul
        li An id on a section, then a href="#/ThatId".
